{
  "summary": "Adds a constructor to `CTransaction` that takes generic input ranges for inputs and outputs, and updates `CTxIn` constructors to accept an optional `CScriptWitness`. It also updates benchmark and test fixtures to construct transactions declaratively rather than mutating a temporary `CMutableTransaction`.",
  "problem": "Constructing immutable `CTransaction` objects currently requires creating and mutating a `CMutableTransaction` first, leading to verbose boilerplate in tests and benchmarks.",
  "evidence": [
    "Part of #36692 (\"Declarative construction of test data\") and designed to support follow-ups like #36694 (author description)",
    "Prevents invariant breaking by copying/moving elements from generic ranges rather than moving `std::vector` containers into place, avoiding external reference backdoors (author description)"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": [
      "#36694"
    ]
  },
  "scope_notes": "Touches core transaction primitive definitions (`CTransaction` and `CTxIn`) to provide constructor ergonomics, then applies the pattern to select test and benchmark call sites.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "CTransaction gains a constructor taking ranges of inputs and outputs directly, and CTxIn constructors gain an optional script witness parameter. This avoids boilerplate CMutableTransaction round-trips when constructing transactions declaratively in tests and benchmarks. The change is part of tracking issue #36692 and provides primitives for PRs like #36694.",
